\section{Transport requirements}{

The client sends a GraphQL request as an HTTP \code{POST} with a JSON body of the
form \verb{\{"query": "...", "variables": \{...\}\}}, which is what \code{ghql} produces.
An endpoint must accept that, and must accept \emph{arbitrary} query documents
rather than only pre-registered (persisted) queries. Ensembl's core,
variation and compara services all satisfy this; the bare \verb{/api/graphql} and
\verb{/api/v1/graphql} paths do not, as they advertise \code{allow: GET} and answer
\code{POST} with HTTP 405.
}

